1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:15,112 --> 00:00:17,680
- Ta!
- Your sister died under suspicious circumstances.

9
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,120
We have to report this to the police.

10
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:21,520
And let the forensic experts determine the cause of her death.

11
00:00:21,558 --> 00:00:23,240
Ta didn't want me to tell anyone about this.

12
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:24,320
I'll investigate it myself.

13
00:00:24,576 --> 00:00:26,320
Is it possible that your sister might have...

14
00:00:26,992 --> 00:00:28,321
maybe she really did take her own life.

15
00:00:28,534 --> 00:00:31,050
The only way to find out what happened to Ta

16
00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:32,560
is for me to become her.

17
00:00:33,142 --> 00:00:34,320
Please don't disappear on me again.

18
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:36,683
And how's the baby?

19
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:38,920
- Ta?
- I had a miscarriage.

20
00:00:39,894 --> 00:00:40,895
I lost the baby.

21
00:00:40,923 --> 00:00:43,280
It's okay. I won't let this happen again.

22
00:00:43,419 --> 00:00:44,420
And as for you,

23
00:00:44,838 --> 00:00:47,600
get a contraceptive implant so you won't get pregnant again.

24
00:00:48,176 --> 00:00:50,250
Hong, who pushed me down the stairs?

25
00:00:50,395 --> 00:00:52,000
Here's what happened.

26
00:00:52,248 --> 00:00:54,254
Mutta, where did you get that ring?

27
00:00:54,403 --> 00:00:55,680
Someone gave it to me.

28
00:00:56,547 --> 00:00:58,800
Jenphop proposed to me with that ring.

29
00:00:58,824 --> 00:01:00,000
How could you possibly have the same ring?

30
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,560
If word of this ever gets out,

31
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:02,920
I'll make every last one of you pay!

32
00:01:04,078 --> 00:01:06,920
When it comes to mistresses, there's no level I won't stoop to!

33
00:01:07,771 --> 00:01:08,772
Ta!

34
00:01:10,358 --> 00:01:12,739
- Are you okay?
- If you don't stay away from my husband,

35
00:01:12,776 --> 00:01:14,130
I'll make sure you suffer again!

36
00:01:15,448 --> 00:01:17,680
I simply got rid of something that had been bothering me.

37
00:01:18,254 --> 00:01:19,480
You hurt my sister!

38
00:01:19,752 --> 00:01:20,880
You bitch, Nopnapha!

39
00:01:24,059 --> 00:01:25,060
Ta.

40
00:01:25,955 --> 00:01:27,880
How's the wound from your fall down the stairs?

41
00:01:28,414 --> 00:01:29,415
Has it healed yet?

42
00:01:29,992 --> 00:01:31,103
The scab has fallen off.

43
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:33,960
It's just a faint scar. It'll fade soon.

44
00:01:38,806 --> 00:01:40,160
I think you should quit your job.

45
00:01:43,062 --> 00:01:45,600
I'm afraid you'll run into her at the ministry and get into another fight.

46
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,531
And you'll have to put up with all the gossip, too.

47
00:01:49,976 --> 00:01:52,160
It's okay. I can handle it.

48
00:01:57,011 --> 00:01:58,012
Wow.

49
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:01,840
Everything looks so delicious.

50
00:02:02,486 --> 00:02:03,760
You're such a good cook.

51
00:02:06,904 --> 00:02:09,432
Once we're finally married,

52
00:02:10,478 --> 00:02:12,560
I'll get to enjoy your cooking at every meal.

53
00:02:13,870 --> 00:02:15,600
I'm definitely going to gain weight, Ta.

54
00:02:16,248 --> 00:02:17,249
Would that be so bad?

55
00:02:18,318 --> 00:02:20,488
I'm going to fatten up both you and our child.

56
00:02:21,294 --> 00:02:22,960
You'll both be nice and chubby.

57
00:02:23,806 --> 00:02:24,920
Come on, Ta.

58
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,846
Why are you bringing up having kids?

59
00:02:27,422 --> 00:02:29,423
Didn't we agree we wouldn't have any children?

60
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,691
I'm getting old. I can't handle raising a child.

61
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:37,880
What if we weren't careful?

62
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:44,641
What do you mean?

63
00:02:49,216 --> 00:02:50,720
I'm already one month pregnant.

64
00:02:53,814 --> 00:02:54,815
What?

65
00:02:56,155 --> 00:02:57,156
Are you serious?

66
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,001
Director?

67
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:00,601
Director.

68
00:03:01,075 --> 00:03:02,250
I love our baby.

69
00:03:03,902 --> 00:03:05,440
I want to have a baby with you.

70
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:08,120
Please don't make me have an abortion.

71
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,601
Please.

72
00:03:10,301 --> 00:03:11,302
Of course not.

73
00:03:12,126 --> 00:03:13,880
Ta, listen.

74
00:03:16,163 --> 00:03:18,280
If you want to keep the baby, I won't force you to do anything.

75
00:03:21,126 --> 00:03:23,250
Ta... Don't worry.

76
00:03:24,875 --> 00:03:26,040
I'll take responsibility.

77
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:27,601
Okay?

78
00:03:31,907 --> 00:03:32,908
Don't worry, sweetheart.

79
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,601
Whoa.

80
00:05:06,579 --> 00:05:08,680
I don't even know which part to be shocked about first.

81
00:05:09,507 --> 00:05:11,508
Mutta's boyfriend was the director.

82
00:05:11,806 --> 00:05:13,880
Then she got pregnant by accident and had a miscarriage.

83
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,201
I really have to admire your sister's courage.

84
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:20,501
Of all the men she could've had an affair with, she chose Nopnapha's husband.

85
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,001
What's so special about her?

86
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,440
I haven't really been following Thai politics.

87
00:05:26,939 --> 00:05:29,080
She's done a pretty good job as a minister.

88
00:05:29,419 --> 00:05:30,640
Everyone's saying

89
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,822
she's going to be the next prime minister.

90
00:05:33,515 --> 00:05:36,050
But behind the scenes, she's shady as hell.

91
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,550
Her father's a mafia boss,

92
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:40,650
so she's used to pulling strings outside the system to play political games.

93
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:44,560
As for your sister's death, it's obvious who was behind it.

94
00:05:51,838 --> 00:05:53,720
The reason Mutta didn't want me telling anyone

95
00:05:54,318 --> 00:05:55,800
or digging into the truth

96
00:05:57,595 --> 00:05:59,040
was probably because she was afraid I'd get hurt too.

97
00:06:00,582 --> 00:06:01,583
You know,

98
00:06:01,968 --> 00:06:03,600
I talked to Mutta every single day.

99
00:06:04,251 --> 00:06:06,150
Yet I never knew any of this.

100
00:06:06,702 --> 00:06:07,703
What the hell...

101
00:06:08,830 --> 00:06:10,360
What kind of sister am I?

102
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:12,400
Don't blame yourself, Munin.

103
00:06:13,187 --> 00:06:15,320
The reason Mutta kept all this from you

104
00:06:15,598 --> 00:06:17,320
was because she didn't want you to worry like this.

105
00:06:25,118 --> 00:06:26,850
We grew up in an orphanage.

106
00:06:29,382 --> 00:06:30,840
All we had was each other.

107
00:06:33,707 --> 00:06:36,180
I thought we were close enough to talk about anything.

108
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:43,161
We even planned to build houses next to each other

109
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:47,200
so we could spend the rest of our lives together.

110
00:06:49,734 --> 00:06:51,460
But she kept so many secrets from me.

111
00:06:56,352 --> 00:06:58,180
She must've had her reasons.

112
00:07:02,243 --> 00:07:03,244
But...

113
00:07:03,875 --> 00:07:05,260
I think I've found a flaw in this theory.

114
00:07:06,819 --> 00:07:08,820
If Nopnapha really ordered your sister's murder,

115
00:07:09,368 --> 00:07:10,800
and you went back to work today,

116
00:07:10,968 --> 00:07:12,500
someone as powerful as her would've known, right?

117
00:07:13,747 --> 00:07:16,440
If she knew, why hasn't she done anything?

118
00:07:17,571 --> 00:07:19,400
Wouldn't she think you're a ghost?

119
00:07:20,702 --> 00:07:21,703
Yeah.

120
00:07:23,155 --> 00:07:24,520
If she really ordered the murder,

121
00:07:25,390 --> 00:07:27,283
why didn't she make sure the body was taken care of?

122
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:29,960
Why leave it in the water for someone to find?

123
00:07:33,613 --> 00:07:34,760
Or maybe...

124
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:37,320
she had nothing to do with it after all.

125
00:07:39,451 --> 00:07:41,480
Ugh, this is giving me a headache.

126
00:07:41,835 --> 00:07:43,880
Can we figure it out later? Let's drink first.

127
00:07:44,459 --> 00:07:45,460
Come on, cheers!

128
00:08:54,966 --> 00:08:55,967
Yes?

129
00:08:57,824 --> 00:08:58,825
Tetris

130
00:09:00,048 --> 00:09:02,560
Hey, why are you still awake?

131
00:09:06,227 --> 00:09:07,360
Come on, now.

132
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:10,600
You don't have to come first in your class this semester.

133
00:09:10,854 --> 00:09:12,240
Let someone else have a turn.

134
00:09:12,998 --> 00:09:14,360
Has Mom come home yet?

135
00:09:16,187 --> 00:09:17,188
Not yet.

136
00:09:17,366 --> 00:09:19,120
She has a cabinet meeting today, so she'll probably be home late.

137
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:22,120
You go ahead and get some sleep.

138
00:09:25,795 --> 00:09:26,796
Sweet dreams.

139
00:09:27,550 --> 00:09:28,551
Daddy loves you.

140
00:09:36,152 --> 00:09:37,153
Night-night.

141
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,170
We are dating.

142
00:09:47,982 --> 00:09:48,983
So she's back.

143
00:09:49,683 --> 00:09:50,760
Have you seen her yet?

144
00:09:53,102 --> 00:09:54,360
You've got quite a nose for trouble.

145
00:09:55,128 --> 00:09:56,250
Just like a dog.

146
00:09:58,648 --> 00:10:00,520
Well, when you've got a womanizing husband, you have to stay alert.

147
00:10:03,056 --> 00:10:04,057
How is she doing?

148
00:10:06,576 --> 00:10:07,577
She lost the baby.

149
00:10:13,419 --> 00:10:14,420
I've never seen a woman smile so wickedly

150
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,920
after hearing that someone had a miscarriage.

151
00:10:20,059 --> 00:10:21,120
If she died,

152
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,401
I'd have an even bigger smile on my face.

153
00:10:34,942 --> 00:10:37,440
Fire her tomorrow so we won't have any more problems.

154
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,600
What other problems could there be?

155
00:10:40,568 --> 00:10:42,250
I've already made her get a contraceptive implant.

156
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:45,360
I guarantee she won't get pregnant again.

157
00:10:46,358 --> 00:10:47,867
I'm not just worried about pregnancy.

158
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,400
I don't want any parasites leeching off you, either.

159
00:10:50,971 --> 00:10:52,572
Because all the money you let her bleed you dry of

160
00:10:52,654 --> 00:10:54,640
- is my money!
- So what if it's your money?

161
00:10:55,438 --> 00:10:57,039
I'm not firing Mutta.

162
00:10:57,619 --> 00:10:59,320
I like having her around. Got a problem with that?

163
00:11:08,059 --> 00:11:09,060
Fine.

164
00:11:23,606 --> 00:11:24,607
Oshi!

165
00:11:26,395 --> 00:11:28,560
I need the men in black to do another job for me.

166
00:11:29,259 --> 00:11:30,640
I'll contact them for you, ma'am.

167
00:11:43,811 --> 00:11:44,958
Don't dwell on it, okay?

168
00:11:45,256 --> 00:11:46,760
Call me anytime if you need anything.

169
00:11:49,422 --> 00:11:50,520
My ride's here.

170
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,201
I'm off now.

171
00:11:52,270 --> 00:11:53,285
Get home safe, okay?

172
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:55,801
Bye-bye.

173
00:11:59,139 --> 00:12:00,400
Soi Ari 10, please.

174
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:02,301
See you.

175
00:12:14,947 --> 00:12:16,448
Northgate Phahonyothin, right?

176
00:12:17,230 --> 00:12:18,231
Yes.

177
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,321
I've just got a bit of a cold.

178
00:12:55,043 --> 00:12:56,044
Excuse me.

179
00:12:56,264 --> 00:12:57,400
This isn't the right way.

180
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,921
Where are you taking me?

181
00:12:59,934 --> 00:13:01,680
Stop the car right now! Stop!

182
00:13:02,136 --> 00:13:03,960
I said stop the car! Stop!

183
00:13:20,678 --> 00:13:21,920
Where do you think you're going?

184
00:13:23,347 --> 00:13:24,348
Well, well, well.

185
00:13:27,086 --> 00:13:28,520
Everybody, please calm down.

186
00:13:29,087 --> 00:13:31,840
Whatever this is about, I'm sure we can work something out.

187
00:13:32,532 --> 00:13:35,560
You'd better stay away from Mr. Jenphop.

188
00:13:37,112 --> 00:13:38,640
Because if you don't,

189
00:13:39,603 --> 00:13:41,250
you'll be seeing a lot more of us.

190
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,601
How about that?

191
00:13:43,310 --> 00:13:46,280
I like them fair-skinned. Come here!

192
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:47,680
- Let go of me!
- Stop fighting!

193
00:13:50,982 --> 00:13:51,983
Let me go!

194
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,160
You've got quite a fight in you, huh?

195
00:14:03,726 --> 00:14:05,024
You won't fight anymore?

196
00:14:23,526 --> 00:14:24,527
Let me go!

197
00:14:24,731 --> 00:14:26,050
How much did she pay you?

198
00:14:26,186 --> 00:14:27,560
I'll pay you double.

199
00:14:30,990 --> 00:14:33,191
It's not often we get our hands on someone this good.

200
00:14:34,446 --> 00:14:35,600
Let us have some fun with you.

201
00:14:41,664 --> 00:14:44,200
I won first prize for my Mother's Day essay.

202
00:14:44,427 --> 00:14:46,200
The teacher wants me to read it at the morning assembly tomorrow.

203
00:14:47,206 --> 00:14:49,407
What did you write? Let me read it.

204
00:14:50,294 --> 00:14:53,120
I'll show you the video of my speech tomorrow instead.

205
00:14:57,126 --> 00:14:58,127
Come in.

206
00:15:03,987 --> 00:15:08,000
Today's mission has been completed, ma'am.

207
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,161
I have AIDS!

208
00:15:48,035 --> 00:15:49,036
I have AIDS!

209
00:15:49,171 --> 00:15:50,320
Don't try to fool me.

210
00:15:51,638 --> 00:15:52,800
I'm his mistress.

211
00:15:53,126 --> 00:15:55,320
How many men do you think I've slept with, huh?

212
00:15:55,515 --> 00:15:56,740
Go ahead and try me if you want.

213
00:16:01,910 --> 00:16:04,700
Tell whoever hired you that you got the job done.

214
00:16:05,275 --> 00:16:07,520
I'll play along. Got it?

215
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,960
This is getting way out of hand, Munin.

216
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:11,921
You need to go to the police right now.

217
00:16:11,974 --> 00:16:14,080
About both what happened to you and your sister.

218
00:16:14,982 --> 00:16:17,014
Nopnapha has way too much power.

219
00:16:17,223 --> 00:16:18,918
Even if I report it, the police won't do a thing.

220
00:16:22,782 --> 00:16:25,500
Then you need to stay out of this and fly back to America.

221
00:16:26,334 --> 00:16:27,896
Go back to your life over there.

222
00:16:28,270 --> 00:16:30,560
Don't throw your life away here. It's not worth it.

223
00:16:30,947 --> 00:16:31,948
No.

224
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:33,960
I've only been pretending to be Mutta for one day,

225
00:16:34,024 --> 00:16:36,000
and I've already been through so much hell.

226
00:16:36,355 --> 00:16:37,971
Mutta had been living like this for so long.

227
00:16:38,472 --> 00:16:39,960
God knows what she must've gone through.

228
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,641
I have to avenge her.

229
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:30,000
[Mr. Sornchai Khoksamroeng (Khem)]

230
00:17:42,021 --> 00:17:43,360
Hello, Sornchai.

231
00:17:44,331 --> 00:17:45,640
I have a job for you.

232
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:47,824
Who do you want me to take care of?

233
00:17:48,336 --> 00:17:50,203
A debtor? A creditor?

234
00:17:50,811 --> 00:17:51,812
A mistress?

235
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:53,520
Or a wife?

236
00:17:55,336 --> 00:17:56,520
My job is much simpler than that.

237
00:17:57,363 --> 00:17:58,840
Just tell me

238
00:17:59,496 --> 00:18:00,800
who hired you yesterday.

239
00:18:01,118 --> 00:18:02,119
Shit!

240
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,521
Sit down.

241
00:18:05,958 --> 00:18:07,000
See that woman over there?

242
00:18:07,616 --> 00:18:08,617
She's a friend of mine.

243
00:18:09,104 --> 00:18:10,422
An undercover cop.

244
00:18:10,896 --> 00:18:12,400
She can call for backup at any moment.

245
00:18:19,899 --> 00:18:20,912
Tell me who hired you.

246
00:18:21,424 --> 00:18:23,245
I want proof of who hired you.

247
00:18:25,264 --> 00:18:26,265
I don't know.

248
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,920
I get my jobs through an agency.

249
00:18:29,344 --> 00:18:30,763
I never deal with the clients directly.

250
00:18:31,990 --> 00:18:33,250
Then give me the agency's number.

251
00:18:35,384 --> 00:18:37,520
I don't have the agency's number or the client's.

252
00:18:38,675 --> 00:18:41,065
They use burner phones to arrange these jobs.

253
00:18:41,566 --> 00:18:42,920
Once the job's done, they destroy the phones.

254
00:18:43,870 --> 00:18:45,320
There's no way you'll track any of them down.

255
00:18:45,371 --> 00:18:47,480
- There has to be a way!
- I told you, there isn't!

256
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:50,240
You'd better talk, or I'll let the police question you.

257
00:18:56,216 --> 00:18:57,217
You bitch!

258
00:19:02,472 --> 00:19:03,570
Well, there is one way.

259
00:19:04,854 --> 00:19:06,855
From the moment a job starts until it's completed,

260
00:19:07,675 --> 00:19:10,600
the agency uses this phone to coordinate everything.

261
00:19:11,312 --> 00:19:13,560
If you want to investigate, that's your window.

262
00:19:22,907 --> 00:19:23,908
What?

263
00:19:23,908 --> 00:19:25,920
You're seriously going to take down Minister Nopnapha?

264
00:19:26,091 --> 00:19:27,300
Have you lost your mind?

265
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:30,040
Yeah, maybe I have.

266
00:19:30,491 --> 00:19:31,960
But she killed my sister.

267
00:19:32,315 --> 00:19:33,961
So I'm going to make her life a living hell.

268
00:19:34,518 --> 00:19:36,960
I'll expose all the evidence of her crimes

269
00:19:37,131 --> 00:19:38,380
for the whole country to see.

270
00:19:39,531 --> 00:19:41,300
And how are you going to get the evidence?

271
00:19:41,478 --> 00:19:44,340
That thug said they destroy everything once the job is done.

272
00:19:45,576 --> 00:19:47,400
I'll make them send someone to attack me again.

273
00:19:47,710 --> 00:19:49,262
That's when we'll get our evidence.

274
00:19:49,672 --> 00:19:51,650
The only way to lure a tiger out of its den

275
00:19:52,131 --> 00:19:53,440
is to provoke it until it gets angry

276
00:19:53,550 --> 00:19:54,960
and comes charging out so we can catch it.

277
00:19:56,638 --> 00:19:59,440
I'm afraid it'll tear you apart before you can catch it.

278
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:01,120
Look what happened to your sister.

279
00:20:01,288 --> 00:20:03,432
You're dealing with one of the most powerful people in the country.

280
00:20:04,611 --> 00:20:06,360
That's why we need to prepare carefully.

281
00:20:08,104 --> 00:20:09,523
And how are you going to provoke her

282
00:20:09,726 --> 00:20:11,534
into sending someone after you again?

283
00:20:12,963 --> 00:20:15,400
I'll do exactly what Mutta did.

284
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:17,801
There's no need to worry about the budget we've spent.

285
00:20:18,078 --> 00:20:19,640
Because we will ensure

286
00:20:19,659 --> 00:20:22,040
that every taxpayer's money is put to the best possible use,

287
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:25,120
in keeping with our ministry's motto:

288
00:20:25,366 --> 00:20:26,670
- Honesty. Transparency.
- [Mrs. Nopnapha Jetsadaphiban]

289
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:28,105
- Fiscal discipline.
- [Minister of Digital Finance]

290
00:20:38,544 --> 00:20:40,720
I'll become the new Mutta for you.

291
00:21:00,166 --> 00:21:01,167
Hello there.

292
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:02,801
Nopnapha.

293
00:21:17,886 --> 00:21:18,887
Veekit.

294
00:21:20,424 --> 00:21:21,425
Veekit.

295
00:21:23,571 --> 00:21:24,572
Veekit!

296
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:26,901
Whoa!

297
00:21:27,390 --> 00:21:28,391
Did you change your hairstyle?

298
00:21:29,208 --> 00:21:30,209
You look different.

299
00:21:30,296 --> 00:21:32,700
Yeah, I felt like becoming a new person.

300
00:21:34,286 --> 00:21:37,360
I came to apologize for what I said the other day.

301
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:39,360
After all those insults, why bother apologizing?

302
00:21:40,486 --> 00:21:41,600
Come on, let me apologize.

303
00:21:42,096 --> 00:21:43,414
I got the wrong idea about you.

304
00:21:44,091 --> 00:21:45,240
And that was just a little misunderstanding?

305
00:21:45,328 --> 00:21:46,680
You even called me an alpaca.

306
00:21:47,166 --> 00:21:48,900
If it had been a big one, would you have called me a macaque?

307
00:21:53,112 --> 00:21:54,250
So what did you misunderstand?

308
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:58,101
I...

309
00:21:58,566 --> 00:21:59,680
Something bad happened to me.

310
00:22:00,118 --> 00:22:01,126
And I thought you were behind it.

311
00:22:01,216 --> 00:22:03,720
Something bad? What happened? Who did it?

312
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:07,640
Don't worry about me.

313
00:22:08,382 --> 00:22:09,600
I'm fine, really.

314
00:22:10,179 --> 00:22:11,960
Anyway, I know who did it now.

315
00:22:12,510 --> 00:22:13,511
I'll deal with it myself.

316
00:22:13,544 --> 00:22:15,811
Come on, Ta.

317
00:22:15,886 --> 00:22:16,887
You can't just leave me hanging like that.

318
00:22:17,027 --> 00:22:18,628
Aren't you going to tell me who did what to you?

319
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:25,700
You know who I've been having trouble with.

320
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:28,701
Aunt Nopnapha?

321
00:22:29,900 --> 00:22:32,120
Why? What did she do to you this time?

322
00:22:37,363 --> 00:22:38,840
Even if I told you, there's nothing you could do.

323
00:22:39,368 --> 00:22:40,369
Let's just say

324
00:22:42,307 --> 00:22:43,440
I'm still alive.

325
00:22:43,900 --> 00:22:44,901
Ta.

326
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:47,101
If you don't want Aunt Nopnapha to hurt you again,

327
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:49,320
just stay away from Uncle Jenphop.

328
00:22:50,192 --> 00:22:51,193
It's that simple.

329
00:22:54,032 --> 00:22:55,080
What if I want her to hurt me?

330
00:23:02,168 --> 00:23:03,169
Ta, are you...

331
00:23:04,820 --> 00:23:05,821
Ta!

332
00:23:06,435 --> 00:23:07,840
Missing me already, Ta? It's still early.

333
00:23:08,464 --> 00:23:09,465
Yes, Director.

334
00:23:09,824 --> 00:23:12,425
But Veekit tried to stop me from seeing you.

335
00:23:14,886 --> 00:23:15,887
Get out! Go on!

336
00:23:16,774 --> 00:23:18,075
I have something to discuss with Ta.

337
00:23:21,758 --> 00:23:22,759
Get out!

338
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:27,801
Oh!

339
00:23:31,395 --> 00:23:32,396
Wait a second.

340
00:23:34,371 --> 00:23:37,582
Is that a new hairstyle for tonight's event?

341
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:39,501
Well then...

342
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:41,760
Let's go somewhere after the event tonight.

343
00:23:43,454 --> 00:23:44,840
Of course, Director.

344
00:23:45,107 --> 00:23:46,720
We haven't done anything in two weeks.

345
00:23:47,411 --> 00:23:49,300
I've been dying to feel your touch again.

346
00:23:53,150 --> 00:23:54,840
I didn't know you could talk so dirty.

347
00:23:55,742 --> 00:23:56,743
I've never heard you talk like that before.

348
00:23:57,859 --> 00:24:00,160
Don't you like it, Director? I'm sorry.

349
00:24:00,206 --> 00:24:01,207
Of course I do.

350
00:24:03,304 --> 00:24:04,305
You should talk like that more often.

351
00:24:06,083 --> 00:24:07,084
It's such a turn-on.

352
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:10,561
Director?

353
00:24:12,368 --> 00:24:14,169
Could I have a drink, please?

354
00:24:17,307 --> 00:24:18,308
Of course.

355
00:24:20,211 --> 00:24:21,480
Someone just gave me a bottle of Moët.

356
00:24:22,419 --> 00:24:24,640
Let's celebrate your return with a drink.

357
00:25:12,142 --> 00:25:13,143
You know, Ta,

358
00:25:14,158 --> 00:25:15,159
I have to tell you something.

359
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:19,180
I missed you like crazy while you were away.

360
00:25:21,587 --> 00:25:23,040
I missed those lips of yours.

361
00:25:28,958 --> 00:25:31,240
Let me go catch up on my work first, Director.

362
00:25:36,366 --> 00:25:37,367
Ta?

363
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,400
I'll see you at the event tonight.

364
00:25:59,016 --> 00:26:00,017
Hey, Auntie.

365
00:26:03,139 --> 00:26:06,360
What's with that hairstyle? It looks so weird.

366
00:26:06,824 --> 00:26:08,125
It's so messy.

367
00:26:10,430 --> 00:26:13,200
It's a modern hairstyle, so it's meant to look a little messy.

368
00:26:13,592 --> 00:26:15,000
Some people just don't get it.

369
00:26:17,368 --> 00:26:18,960
And what time do you call this?

370
00:26:19,302 --> 00:26:20,720
You're only just showing up for work?

371
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:24,300
I went to see the director.

372
00:26:24,982 --> 00:26:26,891
- About what?
- We haven't named it yet.

373
00:26:27,163 --> 00:26:29,164
Let's just say it was personal.

374
00:26:30,827 --> 00:26:32,560
This is a government office.

375
00:26:33,187 --> 00:26:34,680
We're civil servants.

376
00:26:34,966 --> 00:26:36,640
And these are official working hours.

377
00:26:36,923 --> 00:26:39,124
Yet you're using them for personal matters?

378
00:26:40,744 --> 00:26:43,620
Well, I'm working for the director directly.

379
00:26:43,798 --> 00:26:47,000
I have to do whatever he tells me to.

380
00:26:47,272 --> 00:26:50,760
Wow, talk about shameless butt-kissing.

381
00:26:50,995 --> 00:26:54,730
I bet you've licked him all over by now.

382
00:26:56,120 --> 00:26:58,240
Well, everyone wants to suck up to the director.

383
00:26:58,595 --> 00:27:00,120
Don't tell me you two...

384
00:27:00,230 --> 00:27:02,120
don't want to kiss up to him, too.

385
00:27:03,859 --> 00:27:04,860
We…

386
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:07,960
are civil servants with professional ethics.

387
00:27:09,180 --> 00:27:10,181
As for you,

388
00:27:10,576 --> 00:27:11,840
you sleep with him a few times,

389
00:27:12,518 --> 00:27:13,640
and you think you can climb the ladder?

390
00:27:14,166 --> 00:27:15,767
You'll come crashing down soon enough.

391
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:18,000
Take my advice.

392
00:27:18,438 --> 00:27:20,640
Don't even think about getting promoted this way.

393
00:27:20,649 --> 00:27:21,650
It won't get you anywhere.

394
00:27:24,315 --> 00:27:26,640
Thank you for taking the time to warn me

395
00:27:26,843 --> 00:27:28,700
and offer such valuable advice,

396
00:27:29,152 --> 00:27:31,123
even though it's not your job at all.

397
00:27:31,862 --> 00:27:35,240
I'll remember it and try to apply it to my daily life.

398
00:27:39,728 --> 00:27:42,700
Hey, she's actually pretty sweet, you know.

399
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:45,320
See? She's not such a bad girl after all.

400
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:48,401
She listens to us and even thanks us.

401
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:49,881
Sak!

402
00:27:50,718 --> 00:27:51,719
Are you an idiot?

403
00:27:52,526 --> 00:27:54,300
- She just told us to mind our own business!
- Huh?

404
00:27:54,894 --> 00:27:57,520
That Mutta, ever since she came back,

405
00:27:57,800 --> 00:28:00,760
I don't know where she picked up all that attitude,
but she's gotten awfully mouthy.

406
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:02,561
I, for one,

407
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:05,080
can't wait for Mrs. Nopnapha to find out

408
00:28:05,090 --> 00:28:06,091
that she's back.

409
00:28:06,846 --> 00:28:08,920
People really love the Smart ID Card project.

410
00:28:09,304 --> 00:28:11,160
It's revolutionized Thailand's information system.

411
00:28:11,740 --> 00:28:12,920
Especially something people have always hated,

412
00:28:13,744 --> 00:28:15,600
having to photocopy their ID cards.

413
00:28:17,275 --> 00:28:19,720
This project will be our party's legacy for years to come.

414
00:28:20,107 --> 00:28:22,945
It could even help us win the next election.

415
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:24,840
That's why I think

416
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:27,800
instead of our usual 30% kickback from each project,

417
00:28:28,510 --> 00:28:31,440
we should settle for just 15% this time

418
00:28:31,926 --> 00:28:33,520
to ensure the highest quality of work.

419
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,001
Please excuse me.

420
00:29:03,206 --> 00:29:04,207
Where are you going, ma'am?

421
00:29:04,486 --> 00:29:05,920
To wring that bitch's neck.

422
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:08,720
Even after being gang-raped, she still hasn't learned her lesson!

423
00:29:11,552 --> 00:29:13,560
My apologies. The minister has an urgent matter to attend to.

424
00:29:13,620 --> 00:29:14,960
If there's anything you need, you can leave a message with me.

425
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,900
[Ministry of Digital Finance]

426
00:29:51,024 --> 00:29:52,025
Oh!

427
00:29:52,680 --> 00:29:54,200
Minister Nopnapha is here!

428
00:29:54,440 --> 00:29:55,641
This way, ma'am.

429
00:29:55,720 --> 00:29:57,500
Minister Nopnapha is here! Make way!

430
00:29:57,920 --> 00:29:59,021
This way, ma'am.

431
00:30:10,795 --> 00:30:11,796
Aunt Nopnapha?

432
00:30:13,832 --> 00:30:14,833
Where is that bitch?

433
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,001
Who?

434
00:30:18,776 --> 00:30:21,283
Don't play dumb! I'm talking about your mistress!

435
00:30:23,584 --> 00:30:26,040
She's at her desk. Why would she be here?

436
00:30:28,992 --> 00:30:30,400
But this is your desk.

437
00:30:33,163 --> 00:30:34,966
Oh, right. So it is.

438
00:30:36,550 --> 00:30:37,800
Don't mess with me!

439
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:40,512
She's barely back at work, and you're already going at it?

440
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:41,931
Are you really that desperate?

441
00:30:43,560 --> 00:30:45,240
Isn't that perfectly normal?

442
00:30:46,216 --> 00:30:47,650
What's all the fuss about?

443
00:30:48,467 --> 00:30:50,640
And what about that director-general position? Have you put my name forward yet?

444
00:30:51,614 --> 00:30:54,215
You think I'm going to give you that promotion now?

445
00:30:54,950 --> 00:30:56,520
You're already like this as a director.

446
00:30:56,704 --> 00:30:58,720
If you become director-general, why not just start your own harem?

447
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:01,120
Well, can I?

448
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:02,901
- Jenphop!
- Auntie, please.

449
00:31:03,144 --> 00:31:04,145
Could you keep your voices down?

450
00:31:06,648 --> 00:31:07,960
Everyone outside can hear you.

451
00:31:11,891 --> 00:31:13,592
- I'll deal with that bitch myself!
- Hey!

452
00:31:13,651 --> 00:31:14,652
Aunt Nopnapha, please don't.

453
00:31:17,043 --> 00:31:19,280
Just wait here. I'll go get her for you.

454
00:31:32,931 --> 00:31:33,932
Meow.

455
00:31:35,678 --> 00:31:37,600
What's that hairstyle Mutta's sporting?

456
00:31:39,704 --> 00:31:41,240
It's this iconic style.

457
00:31:41,448 --> 00:31:44,440
Orn-in's haircut from Mia Luang, you know?

458
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:46,341
Oh, right.

459
00:31:48,139 --> 00:31:49,140
Come on, come on.

460
00:31:50,672 --> 00:31:52,720
Working in the civil service sure is exhausting.

461
00:31:53,310 --> 00:31:55,120
Yeah, I've been stapling all day.

462
00:31:59,700 --> 00:32:00,880
Veekit.

463
00:32:01,582 --> 00:32:03,200
You came all the way here to see me?

464
00:32:03,448 --> 00:32:05,176
Is there anything I can do for you?

465
00:32:06,446 --> 00:32:09,000
Move aside, honey. He's here to see me.

466
00:32:11,144 --> 00:32:14,645
Oh, Veekit, darling. About those documents I'm drafting for the director,

467
00:32:14,650 --> 00:32:16,680
I'll bring them to your desk as soon as they're ready.

468
00:32:17,187 --> 00:32:19,240
You two really have wild imaginations, don't you?

469
00:32:19,918 --> 00:32:21,480
Veekit, darling.

470
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:24,240
You're here to invite me to tonight's fundraising event, aren't you?

471
00:32:24,392 --> 00:32:27,488
Okay, I accept.

472
00:32:27,500 --> 00:32:28,601
I'm actually here to see Ta.

473
00:32:30,300 --> 00:32:31,301
Move aside.

474
00:32:34,130 --> 00:32:36,131
- You're pretty full of yourself, aren't you?
- Thank you.

475
00:32:38,384 --> 00:32:40,385
Ta, she wants to see you.

476
00:32:41,814 --> 00:32:42,815
Who?

477
00:32:46,171 --> 00:32:47,372
You know, the minister.

478
00:32:51,190 --> 00:32:53,200
Minister Nopnapha

479
00:32:53,982 --> 00:32:56,440
wants to speak to me privately?

480
00:33:00,904 --> 00:33:04,000
Please apologize to her for me. I'm busy.

481
00:33:05,542 --> 00:33:08,262
Wow!

482
00:33:08,843 --> 00:33:12,000
Where did you get all that nerve?

483
00:33:12,182 --> 00:33:15,000
How dare you say you're too busy for Minister Nopnapha?

484
00:33:17,216 --> 00:33:18,960
I just want to finish my work.

485
00:33:19,360 --> 00:33:21,120
I don't want to be a burden to anyone.

486
00:33:24,916 --> 00:33:28,920
Or are you afraid to face her again

487
00:33:29,250 --> 00:33:31,520
because she might slap you again?

488
00:33:37,155 --> 00:33:38,880
You've got some nerve, young lady.

489
00:33:39,507 --> 00:33:41,480
You're the first person in history

490
00:33:41,600 --> 00:33:43,680
to dare defy Minister Nopnapha.

491
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,601
You did the right thing.

492
00:33:50,147 --> 00:33:52,720
Work responsibilities come first, right?

493
00:34:03,462 --> 00:34:04,463
You know,

494
00:34:05,430 --> 00:34:07,480
Mutta's been acting a little strange lately.

495
00:34:08,459 --> 00:34:10,960
She's gotten a lot fiercer.

496
00:34:11,707 --> 00:34:13,190
I thought I was the only one who noticed.

497
00:34:13,456 --> 00:34:15,960
What kind of nun taught her meditation?

498
00:34:16,341 --> 00:34:17,342
Exactly.

499
00:34:18,149 --> 00:34:21,450
Maybe that haircut changed her whole personality.

500
00:34:21,579 --> 00:34:22,640
Why don't you get one too?

501
00:34:23,106 --> 00:34:24,520
You should get one yourself.

502
00:34:26,019 --> 00:34:29,000
- What about that wagon-sized Titan?
- He's not doing it. Leave him alone.

503
00:34:29,100 --> 00:34:30,101
Come on, get back to work.

504
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:36,712
She's deliberately trying to provoke me.

505
00:34:37,260 --> 00:34:38,320
I'm glad you realize that, ma'am.

506
00:34:38,755 --> 00:34:40,150
So don't play into her hands.

507
00:34:41,832 --> 00:34:43,300
Please try to stay calm, ma'am.

508
00:34:44,056 --> 00:34:46,920
I don't want a repeat of what happened outside the ministry.

509
00:34:47,432 --> 00:34:50,080
Covering up a scandal like that isn't easy.

510
00:34:51,987 --> 00:34:53,360
Then tell me, Touch.

511
00:34:53,581 --> 00:34:55,840
What am I supposed to do with that bitch?

512
00:34:56,742 --> 00:34:58,243
She disappeared for so long.

513
00:34:58,743 --> 00:35:00,120
I thought it was all over.

514
00:35:00,395 --> 00:35:04,160
But no, she's crawled out of her grave to torment me again.

515
00:35:04,654 --> 00:35:06,880
That mistress is damn near impossible to kill!

516
00:35:13,654 --> 00:35:15,166
I have to be honest with you.

517
00:35:15,300 --> 00:35:17,320
Marital problems aren't exactly my area of expertise.

518
00:35:19,118 --> 00:35:21,160
But I don't believe in using violence.

519
00:35:21,822 --> 00:35:24,400
I believe in talking things through peacefully.

520
00:35:25,400 --> 00:35:27,601
I've tried talking to that bitch countless times.

521
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:29,896
But she never listens to reason.

522
00:35:30,900 --> 00:35:32,320
I meant talking to the director.

523
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:36,080
Perhaps getting a divorce

524
00:35:36,304 --> 00:35:37,840
would be the best solution.

525
00:35:40,784 --> 00:35:42,120
Congratulations

526
00:35:42,150 --> 00:35:45,000
to Minister Nopnapha and her family

527
00:35:45,100 --> 00:35:48,160
on receiving this year's Outstanding Family Award.

528
00:35:48,283 --> 00:35:52,120
You're truly a role model for families across Thailand.

529
00:35:52,640 --> 00:35:53,641
No.

530
00:35:54,220 --> 00:35:55,321
I can't get divorced.

531
00:36:16,512 --> 00:36:18,300
I call shotgun!

532
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:20,000
Your seat's back there.

533
00:36:23,259 --> 00:36:24,260
After you.

534
00:36:31,907 --> 00:36:34,008
- Hello, Veekit.
